  "overview": "Anguilla is the northernmost of the Leeward Islands, a flat coral and limestone island about 16 miles long and 3 miles wide, just nine miles north of St. Martin. What it lacks in mountains it makes up for in sand: there are 33 beaches, every one of them public, and most are calm, clear and gentle. It is a self-governing British Overseas Territory where English is spoken, and it calls itself the culinary capital of the Caribbean, with more than 100 restaurants from fine dining to beach bars. People come for that rare mix of quiet and polish: long days on Shoal Bay or Meads Bay, boat trips out to the offshore cays, lobster and crayfish fresh from local waters, and dinners with the sea only a few steps away.",
