  "sourceNotes": "FACTS (all Anguilla Tourist Board, ivisitanguilla.com, read Oct 2026): northernmost Leeward Island, 150 miles east of Puerto Rico, nine miles north of St. Martin (/getting-to-anguilla); 16 x 3 miles, drive end to end in about 45 minutes, drive on the left, temporary Anguillian license required, coral and limestone, flat (/transportation, /faq); 33 beaches, all public, parking never an issue, most beaches placid and calm, Little Bay reachable only by boat (/beaches, /faq); British Overseas Territory, English, 100+ restaurants, lobster and crayfish (/faq); 'culinary capital of the Caribbean' is the board's own phrase (homepage); Wallblake House 1785, only surviving plantation house; Island Harbour and Scilly Cay; Prickly Pear restaurants Agatha's and Johnno's; West End resorts incl. Four Seasons, Aurora, Malliouhana; Zemi Beach House at Shoal Bay East (/explore-our-island); boat racing is the national sport (/boating). GETTING THERE: MIA–AXA on American Airlines, SJU connections (Seaborne, Tradewind, etc.), SXM seven-minute flight via Anguilla Air Services, public ferry to Blowing Point (/getting-to-anguilla). The board lists MIA–AXA under its 'one-stop' heading; whether it is nonstop on a given date was not confirmed, so the copy says 'service from Miami'. Ferry crossing time not stated by the board, so left out. AXA airport location: board /faq. STAYS: Cap Juluca mile-long crescent from our library description; Malliouhana between Meads Bay and Turtle Cove, Aurora on Rendezvous Bay with Greg Norman course, Four Seasons between Barnes and Meads Bay: from our own Anguilla guide plus resort sites, not independently re-checked this pass. CLIMATE: Anguilla has no published WMO or NOAA climate normals (Anguilla is not in the WMO 1991–2020 collection, and NOAA daily data for AXA records daytime hours only, which skews the lows). Used WMO Climatological Standard Normals 1991–2020 for Princess Juliana International Airport, Sint Maarten (WMO 78866), published by NOAA NCEI (accession 0253808), converted from °C. The two airports are about 15 miles apart at the same latitude, but flag this to clients as the nearest station. PHOTOS: Hero: Sandy Ground bay with moored boats, daylight, 2000x1188, Anguilla Tourist Board (ivisitanguilla.com); a few tiny figures on the beach. Gallery 1: overhead aerial of Shoal Bay East, 2027x1350, Zemi Beach House official site (served from its Rackspace CDN); resort roofs and pool along the bottom edge, crop from top if needed. Gallery 2: Maundays Bay aerial at golden hour, 2580x1299, Belmond Cap Juluca official page; resort villas fill about half the frame (f_auto URL may serve WebP/AVIF to browsers). Most large ivisitanguilla.com images carry an 'anguilla' corner logo and were rejected. Alternates: Sandy Island aerial (ivisitanguilla.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/sandy-island.jpg, has umbrellas and beach bar), Rendezvous Bay from Aurora Anguilla (resort in foreground).\nPhotos: landscape https://explorajourneys.com/us/en/destinations-globe/caribbean/city-guides/anguilla-escapism; local https://www.fourseasons.com/anguilla/experiences/ (Four Seasons Resort and Residences Anguilla, 'Power & Performance Escape - Elite Private Charter')\nTemperature strip: Average daily high and low in °F, measured at Princess Juliana International Airport, St. Maarten, on neighboring St. Maarten, the nearest official station.\nReview 2026-10-03: REVIEW 2026-10-03. byPlane: AXA on the immediate outskirts of The Valley (ivisitanguilla.com/faq); AXA to Four Seasons (Barnes Bay/Meads Bay, West End) 'Travel Time 20 minutes by car', SXM to Blowing Point '25 to 30 minutes by boat', Blowing Point to resort 15 to 20 minutes by car (fourseasons.com/anguilla/getting-here, read Oct 2026); SXM to AXA seven-minute flight and public ferry from Marigot eight times daily (ivisitanguilla.com/getting-to-anguilla). byCar: 16 miles end to end in about forty-five minutes (ivisitanguilla.com/transportation). Highlights: Sandy Island restaurant, hammocks, lounges and snorkeling (ivisitanguilla.com/explore-our-island); Wallblake House 1785 and only surviving plantation house, Prickly Pear restaurants Agatha's and Johnno's (same page); boat racing national sport (/boating); Little Bay reachable only by boat, most beaches placid and calm (/beaches). Overview facts re-checked: northernmost Leeward Island, nine miles north of St. Martin (/getting-to-anguilla); 16 x 3 miles, 33 beaches, 100+ restaurants, 'Self-governing, British Overseas Territory', crayfish and lobster (/faq). Tip: left-hand driving, temporary Anguillian license US$25 valid three months (/transportation). Climate cross-check: Meteo Curacao summary for Princess Juliana Airport 1971-2000 (meteo.cw CLIM_SUM_SXM.pdf) gives Jan 83.5/73.8°F, Jun 88.3/77.4°F, Aug 89.1/79.2°F, Dec 84.6/75.0°F (1961-1990 table); strip values (1991-2020 WMO normals) agree within about 1 to 2°F, consistent with the warmer later period. Stays: Aurora's 18-hole Greg Norman course on Rendezvous Bay confirmed (Salamander Hotels announcement, Virtuoso listing). PHOTOS: the hero/photo notes above are stale. Current hero = Shoal Bay East overhead aerial, 2027x1350, Zemi Beach House official site (Rackspace CDN), accepted by Wilson. PHOTO 1 = Little Bay cliffs and cove, 2000x1333, Explora Journeys Anguilla city guide (explorajourneys.com/us/en/destinations-globe/caribbean/city-guides/anguilla-escapism). PHOTO 2 = private speedboat anchored off a sand cay, Four Seasons Anguilla experiences page ('Power & Performance Escape - Elite Private Charter'); same image AIL_808 now served from press.fourseasons.com (3000x1686) because the www.fourseasons.com img-opt URL returned 403 Access Denied to browser-like requests. All photo and stays image URLs return 200 image/* with and without Referer: https://www.wanderbywilson.com/.\nThings to do photos (2026-10-03): item 0: https://explorajourneys.com/us/en/destinations-globe/caribbean/city-guides/anguilla-escapism (Shoal Bay Coastal Connection excursion card); item 1: https://pricklypearanguilla.com/ (Prickly Pear Bar & Restaurant, i.e. Agatha's, own site); item 2: Four Seasons Resort Anguilla image library (AIL_193, original https://press.fourseasons.com/content/dam/fourseasons/images/web/AIL/AIL_193_original.jpg, 2000x3000 portrait); URL is Four Seasons' own image service cropping it square; item 3: https://www.mysandyisland.com/ (Sandy Island restaurant's own site; original 4703x3527)\nThings to do changes: Dropped 'Tour Wallblake House…': no compliant photo exists. The house has no working official site (wallblake.ai is down) and every usable image sits on Wikimedia, tourism-board or personal blog pages; none of the cruise lines, SmartFlyer, Virtuoso, the featured hotels or Unsplash show it. Also note the item's 1785 date conflicts with sources that give 1787. Dropped 'Catch a boat race…': no allowed source has a photo of Anguilla's racing sloops (only Instagram, Facebook, blogs and a 550px Zemi stock image of dinghies). Searched for replacements (Meads Bay, Sandy Ground/Road Bay, Elvis' Beach Bar, Blanchard's, salt picking, Dog Island, Cavannagh Cave) but none had a photo that was both clearly identifiable and up to standard, so both items were dropped, leaving 4.\nNo new or replaced items.",
