  "overview": "Aspen sits high in Colorado's Roaring Fork Valley, a silver-mining boomtown that grew to more than 12,000 residents before the silver crash of 1893 emptied it out. Skiing and the arrival of Walter and Elizabeth Paepcke in the late 1940s sparked a revival built on what they called the Aspen Idea: mind, body and spirit in balance. That spirit is still the draw. Winter brings four mountains, Aspen Mountain, Aspen Highlands, Buttermilk and Snowmass, and an après scene to match. Summer brings the Aspen Music Festival, wildflowers, and hikes beneath the Maroon Bells, peaks that rise above 14,000 feet. In between is a compact, walkable town of serious restaurants, galleries and shopping.",
