  "overview": "Madrid is the capital of Spain, a city of grand boulevards and green parks on the banks of the Manzanares River. Its first written record dates to 865, when Emir Muhammad I ordered a fortress built at a village called Mayrit. Today the Royal Palace, with more than 3,000 rooms, stands on the western edge of the old town and is still the official residence of the Spanish royal family. To the east, the Paseo del Prado holds three of the world's great art museums, the Prado, the Thyssen-Bornemisza and the Reina Sofía, within two kilometres of one another, and in 2021 UNESCO named the boulevard and El Retiro Park a World Heritage Site. People come for the art, for long meals in taverns that have been serving for centuries, and for a city that comes alive after dark, where dinner rarely starts before ten.",
