  "sourceNotes": "FACTS (esmadrid.com, Madrid's official tourism site, read Oct 2026): first record 865, Emir Muhammad I, fortress at Mayrit on the Manzanares; Royal Palace on the site of the old Alcázar on the city's western border (esmadrid.com/en/history-madrid). Royal Palace over 3,000 rooms, no longer the royal family's home but still their official residence; Changing of the Guard Wednesdays and Saturdays, Solemn Changing first Wednesday of the month except Jan, Aug, Sep (esmadrid.com/en/tourist-information/royal-palace). Paintings by Velázquez, Goya, Rubens, El Greco, Caravaggio (spain.info/en/places-of-interest/royal-palace-madrid/). Prado, Thyssen-Bornemisza and Reina Sofía within two kilometres; Paseo del Prado and El Retiro declared UNESCO World Heritage (Landscape of Light) July 2021 (esmadrid.com/en/madrid-neighbourhoods/paseo-arte; esmadrid.com/en/landscape-light-paseo-prado-and-retiro-park). Guernica at the Reina Sofía since 1992 (museoreinasofia.es). El Retiro over 125 hectares, rowing boats on the lake (esmadrid.com/en/tourist-information/parque-del-retiro). Palacio de Cristal built 1887, glass and cast iron, used by the Reina Sofía for temporary exhibitions (esmadrid.com/en/tourist-information/palacio-de-cristal). Mercado de San Miguel opened May 1916, cast-iron, a stone's throw from Plaza Mayor (esmadrid.com/en/shopping/mercado-de-san-miguel). Botín founded 1725 on Calle Cuchilleros, oldest restaurant in the world per Guinness Book of Records (botin.es/en/conoce-botin/historia-y-evolucion-de-botin/). 'Madrid is open 24 hours a day' and centuries-old taverns (spain.info/en/top/travel-ave-madrid/; esmadrid.com/en/culinary-journey-through-madrids-centuries-old-restaurants-and-taverns). Toledo about 30 minutes by high-speed train from Atocha (spain.info/en/route/explore-spain-on-high-speed-trains/; spain.info/en/discover-spain/day-trips-from-madrid/). BY PLANE: Metro Line 8 Nuevos Ministerios to the airport, 12 minutes to T1–T3 and under 20 to T4; taxi fixed rate between airport and city centre inside the M-30 (esmadrid.com/en/getting-madrid-plane). No official airport-to-centre drive time found, so none quoted. BY TRAIN (spain.info/en/route/explore-spain-on-high-speed-trains/): Madrid–Barcelona from 2 hr 30 min non-stop; Madrid–Seville from 2 hr 30 min; Madrid–Valencia from 1 hr 50 min (the same page's intro says 'about 100 minutes'; the route figure is used). BY CAR: Toledo 60 minutes via the A-42 (esmadrid.com/en/trips-toledo); Segovia 70 minutes via the A-6 and AP-6 (esmadrid.com/en/trips-segovia). CLIMATE and STAYS unchanged from the previous entry; climate source not re-checked this pass.\nTemperature strip: Average daily high and low in °F.\nPhotos: landscape https://unsplash.com/s/photos/palacio-real-de-madrid; local https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/madrid/hotel-ritz/explore (Toledo Farm Experience 4x4)\nMAD to centre about 25–35 min by taxi, flat fare inside the M-30 (Welcome Pickups, LUGGit, madrid-tourist-guide.com).\nReview 2026-10-03: REVIEW 2026-10-03. PHOTO 2 replaced: Mandarin Oriental Ritz, Madrid experience 'Out-of-Hours Museo Nacional Thyssen-Bornemisza Tour' (private themed after-hours tour), image https://media.ffycdn.net/eu/mandarin-oriental-hotel-group/NBztuZVkFryRMv9S3PA8.jpg, 3000x2000, empty galleries in daylight, no people or text; appears on https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/madrid/hotel-ritz/explore and .../explore/out-of-hours-museo-nacional-thyssen-bornemisza-tour; HTTP 200 image/jpeg with and without Referer. Rejected: Toledo 4x4 (an hour out, not luxury-reading), Rosewood Villa Magna experience images (all portrait), Chinchón (plain town square), Mantequerías Bravo tasting (bottle labels/logos). Palacio de Cristal closed since May 2023 for structural restoration until 2027 (elespanol.com 2024-06-01; vidademadrid.com), so the highlight was replaced. Retiro lake rowing boats and Monument to Alfonso XII watching over the lake (esmadrid.com/en/tourist-information/parque-del-retiro). Corral de la Morería opened 25 May 1956, restaurant Michelin-starred since 2019 (corraldelamoreria.com/en/about-us/; esmadrid.com/en/nightlife/corral-moreria). CLIMATE: AEMET, Madrid Retiro station, normals 1981-2010 (aemet.es valoresclimatologicos l=3195), mean max/min converted from °C and rounded; previous strip differed by 1 to 2 °F in Apr to Aug and Oct to Dec. STAYS notes: Four Seasons in Centro Canalejas, seven historic buildings near Puerta del Sol (esmadrid.com/en/accommodation/four-seasons-hotel-madrid); Mandarin Oriental Ritz opened 1910, Plaza de la Lealtad 5 beside the Prado (mandarinoriental.com/en/madrid/hotel-ritz; esmadrid.com/en/accommodation/mandarin-oriental-ritz); Rosewood Villa Magna at Paseo de la Castellana 22, Salamanca (esmadrid.com/en/accommodation/rosewood-villa-magna). None of the three is in data.js, so their images stay; all three image URLs return 200 with and without Referer. Trains cross-checked: Renfe fastest Madrid-Valencia about 1 hour 40 minutes, Seville about 2 hours 20 minutes; spain.info figures kept. Airport: esmadrid.com gives 12 km and Metro times but no drive time.\nPhotos picked by Wilson 2026-10-03: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1663963475501-9a0c47faf39a?fm=jpg&q=90\nThings to do photos (2026-10-03): item 0: https://unsplash.com/photos/olfgV8c-hEw; item 1: https://unsplash.com/photos/8FihBS6IJ1g; item 2: https://unsplash.com/photos/z-OQvRqf8rA; item 3: https://www.corraldelamoreria.com/en/flamenco-show/; item 4: https://botin.es/en/conoce-botin/; item 5: https://unsplash.com/photos/OaqkajLlXLY\nNo items replaced or added.",
