  "overview": "Seville is the capital of Andalusia, in southern Spain, set along the Guadalquivir River. At the heart of its old centre, three monuments were named a UNESCO World Heritage Site together in 1987. The cathedral is the largest Gothic cathedral in the world, and its bell tower, the Giralda, began life as a minaret. The Real Alcázar is the oldest royal palace in Europe still in use and remains the official residence of the Spanish royal family in Seville. The Archivo de Indias keeps original documents signed by Columbus and Magellan. Across the river, Triana is the neighbourhood where the city's ceramics and flamenco traditions have their roots. People come for the monuments, for the tiled Plaza de España, built for the Ibero-American Exposition of 1929, and for evenings spent moving from bar to bar for tapas.",
